{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794543404142,"sessionID":"ses_e2ce11fa0ffeKrU1dSi2GXzG1K","part":{"partID":"prt_1d31f41ef002l2n31SeDqcHdP7","sessionID":"ses_e2ce11fa0ffeKrU1dSi2GXzG1K","messageID":"msg_1d31f073f001lHEiSd3Z3Qwt8d","type":"tool","id":"call_809fd87cf2964bf486984d5d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '109p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- [ ] T005 Insert the ranked `run` command instead of the helper (`FU`, `FHT`). In `FU`: (1) add `COMMAND_ROWS` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'` and `genericRepairCue` to the import from `'./doctor-helper-handoff.js'`. (2) Right above the comment block that precedes `export function applyDoctorHelperHandoff(`, add `export function runnableDoctorBridgeId(runnable: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): string | undefined` with this body: for each `[id, row]` of `Object.entries(COMMAND_ROWS)`, skip it unless `id.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX)`, `row.command === runnable` and `row.policy === 'run'`, and return `id` when `projection.skills.some((skill) => skill.id === id)`. After the loop return `undefined`. Its comment says the ranker names a runnable such as `/doctor:agents-md check`, and this returns that bridge when it runs without asking and the projection holds it. (3) Replace the four comment lines above `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` with: `// A doctor problem described in other words than a bridge's own phrases reaches`, `// no doctor bridge. When none passes and none was typed, /doctor:helper's ranker`, `// decides whether the prompt is a doctor problem. If it is, the command it ranks`, `// first passes when that command runs without asking, and the helper passes`, `// otherwise. A plain request for a repair route with no ranked command and no`, `// passing skill also gets the helper.`. (4) In the function, replace `if (!match) return [...ranked];` with `if (!match && (skillPasses || !genericRepairCue(context.prompt))) return [...ranked];`, and prefix the next condition with `match && ` so it reads `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. (5) Before `const existing =` add `const handoffId = (match ? runnableDoctorBridgeId(match.runnable, context.projection) : undefined) ?? DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID;` and `const handoffSkill = context.projection.skills.find((skill) => skill.id === handoffId) ?? helperSkill;`. (6) In `existing`, in the `skill:` field of `handoff` and in the `ranked.filter` of `withHandoff`, use `handoffId` where the code reads `DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID`. Set `lifecycleStatus` from `handoffSkill`. (7) Make `reason` read `doctor helper hand-off: /doctor:helper ranks ${match.runnable} first for this problem` when `match` is set and the plain string `doctor helper hand-off: a repair request with no matched doctor route` when it is null. Create `FHT` under the frozen regime of `$ADV/tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` (its `freezeEvalEnv`, its fake `Date` at the `capturedAt` of `scorer-eval-baseline.json` and `scoreAdvisorPrompt` imported after the freeze). Cases on `result.recommendations` ids in order: `confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted` starts with `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled` starts with `command-doctor-ci-report`, `my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why` starts with `system-deep-loop` then `command-doctor-deep-loop`, `I have a problem and want the right repair path suggested with reasons` starts with `command-doctor-helper`, `much appreciated, that fixed the problem completely` holds no id that starts with `command-doctor-` and `I have a problem with my CSS layout` holds no id that starts with `command-doctor-`. Add pure cases for `runnableDoctorBridgeId` with `{ skills: [{ id: 'command-doctor-agents-md-check' }, { id: 'command-doctor-git-hooks' }] } as unknown as AdvisorProjection`: `/doctor:agents-md check` gives `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `/doctor:git hooks` gives undefined (policy `ask`) and `/doctor:ci report` gives undefined (not in that projection). Verify: `VFHT` reports 0 failed, `VDHT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T005 Insert the ranked `run` command instead of the helper (`FU`, `FHT`). In `FU`: (1) add `COMMAND_ROWS` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'` and `genericRepairCue` to the import from `'./doctor-helper-handoff.js'`. (2) Right above the comment block that precedes `export function applyDoctorHelperHandoff(`, add `export function runnableDoctorBridgeId(runnable: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): string | undefined` with this body: for each `[id, row]` of `Object.entries(COMMAND_ROWS)`, skip it unless `id.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX)`, `row.command === runnable` and `row.policy === 'run'`, and return `id` when `projection.skills.some((skill) => skill.id === id)`. After the loop return `undefined`. Its comment says the ranker names a runnable such as `/doctor:agents-md check`, and this returns that bridge when it runs without asking and the projection holds it. (3) Replace the four comment lines above `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` with: `// A doctor problem described in other words than a bridge's own phrases reaches`, `// no doctor bridge. When none passes and none was typed, /doctor:helper's ranker`, `// decides whether the prompt is a doctor problem. If it is, the command it ranks`, `// first passes when that command runs without asking, and the helper passes`, `// otherwise. A plain request for a repair route with no ranked command and no`, `// passing skill also gets the helper.`. (4) In the function, replace `if (!match) return [...ranked];` with `if (!match && (skillPasses || !genericRepairCue(context.prompt))) return [...ranked];`, and prefix the next condition with `match && ` so it reads `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. (5) Before `const existing =` add `const handoffId = (match ? runnableDoctorBridgeId(match.runnable, context.projection) : undefined) ?? DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID;` and `const handoffSkill = context.projection.skills.find((skill) => skill.id === handoffId) ?? helperSkill;`. (6) In `existing`, in the `skill:` field of `handoff` and in the `ranked.filter` of `withHandoff`, use `handoffId` where the code reads `DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID`. Set `lifecycleStatus` from `handoffSkill`. (7) Make `reason` read `doctor helper hand-off: /doctor:helper ranks ${match.runnable} first for this problem` when `match` is set and the plain string `doctor helper hand-off: a repair request with no matched doctor route` when it is null. Create `FHT` under the frozen regime of `$ADV/tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` (its `freezeEvalEnv`, its fake `Date` at the `capturedAt` of `scorer-eval-baseline.json` and `scoreAdvisorPrompt` imported after the freeze). Cases on `result.recommendations` ids in order: `confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted` starts with `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled` starts with `command-doctor-ci-report`, `my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why` starts with `system-deep-loop` then `command-doctor-deep-loop`, `I have a problem and want the right repair path suggested with reasons` starts with `command-doctor-helper`, `much appreciated, that fixed the problem completely` holds no id that starts with `command-doctor-` and `I have a problem with my CSS layout` holds no id that starts with `command-doctor-`. Add pure cases for `runnableDoctorBridgeId` with `{ skills: [{ id: 'command-doctor-agents-md-check' }, { id: 'command-doctor-git-hooks' }] } as unknown as AdvisorProjection`: `/doctor:agents-md check` gives `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `/doctor:git hooks` gives undefined (policy `ask`) and `/doctor:ci report` gives undefined (not in that projection). Verify: `VFHT` reports 0 failed, `VDHT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '109p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794543403503,"end":1794543404142}}}}
